        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "35-6-1-1 If there are extenuating circumstances, i.e., extended out of state or foreign travel, or other unavoidable circumstances, more than five (5) days of bereavement leave will be granted. In such instances, the leave will be deducted from personal or accrued sick leave. If such leaves are exhausted, the teacher will reimburse the District at the substitute rate of pay for the days used. This reimbursement will be made even if no substitute is required.",
